{"title":"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/2/75212ff6ab19289ae214e99f1f22526e34f9023f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x-200)(4x+1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e561d8bca3fd8b55b65c1b7f6d1f2cb0d911d996.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\omega = \\tan^{-1}(\\alpha) + \\tan^{-1}(\\beta) + \\tan^{-1} (\\gamma).\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"19\" /> The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fa0a0e873426976a635b5ace19eef7a3b2c5b91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\omega)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Determine the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7ebc9435cf037e230c3dea173d52a1c4a4172c10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /> are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46a2163e96d09912f1d3d00f2f23d82a96b240c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(x-200)(x+1/4)-1/4 = x^3 - \\frac{799}{4}x^2 - 50x - \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"406\" height=\"38\" />. By Vieta's formulas, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/e/cee372a6749346c8ef376cfd09dc68f2177b1629.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\frac{799}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"131\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/65074af7b5e5805f97086ed9499bc3d17fd4381f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = -50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59d647d8613109cbbfe59dfd718314e52d6dabf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Now, by tangent addition formulas, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be9a3e056e87201acb9767e7925c6ad998b77ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\omega) = \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma - \\alpha\\beta\\gamma}{1 - \\alpha\\beta - \\beta\\gamma - \\gamma\\alpha}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"221\" height=\"41\" />. Substituting Vieta's formulas, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/4857720fb8346d3140199fef9ed3452a46a41357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\omega) = \\frac{\\frac{799}{4} - \\frac{1}{4}}{1 - (-50)} = \\frac{\\frac{798}{4}}{51} = \\frac{133}{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"264\" height=\"45\" />. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac22a667ab8a79bb730f44ee1e9436049ed9b528.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$133 + 34 = \\boxed{167}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"132\" height=\"25\" /> and we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005\">Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t={{{source}}}\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redl